      "side": 1,
      "message": "Verified locally with `bazel build //tools:full_build`\n\nhttps://paste.googleplex.com/4900750359134208\n\nThe code compiles because `//src/cpu:cpu_hdrs` is a `skia_filegroup` that gets bundled into `//src/core:core_priv_hdrs` (the same pattern as `//src/capture:capture_hdrs`). \n\n```\nskia_filegroup(\n    name \u003d \"capture_hdrs\",\n    srcs \u003d [\n        \"SkCapture.h\",\n        \"SkCaptureCanvas.h\",\n        \"SkCaptureManager.h\",\n    ],\n    visibility \u003d [\"//src/core:__pkg__\"],\n)\n```\nInternal modules like `//src/pdf` and `//src/svg` depend on `//src/core:core_priv`, which exports `core_priv_hdrs` to internal Skia targets while keeping it in srcs for external consumers of //:core.",
